  "content": {
    "title": "Who's on 'Saturday Night Live' tonight? What to know about April 11 show",
    "text": "April 11, 2026, 3:00 p.m. ETTwo Oscar nominations and one Emmy win later, Colman Domingo is ready for his \"Saturday Night Live\" debut.The \"Euphoria\" star, who knows a thing or two about cracking jokes, will be taking the 8H stage alongside Brazilian singer-songwriter Anitta. The duo will be appearing on \"SNL\" for the first time on April 11.In addition to starring alongside \"SNL\" alum Tina Fey in \"The Four Seasons\" and portraying Joe Jackson in the upcoming biopic \"Michael\", Domingo was once a performer on Logo TV's \"The Big Gay Sketch Show\".According to NBC Insider, his \"most famous bit from 'The Big Gay Sketch Show' was an excellent Maya Angelou impression, which he wielded to read Craigslist ads.\"\"Finally. Back to my sketch history,\" Domingo wrote in a March 26 X post. \"We will have fun.\"Here's what to know about the April 11 show, including how to watch.Who's on 'SNL' tonight?\"SNL\" emcee Colman Domingo will be sharing the stage with Anitta, who is this week's musical guest. The \"Pinterest\" singer has released seven studio albums, and her eighth, EQUILIBRIVM, is due on April 16.How to watch 'SNL'?New episodes of \"Saturday Night Live\" air Saturday nights at 11:30 p.m. ET / 8:30 p.m. PT on NBC, with episodes streaming the next day on Peacock. Old \"SNL\" episodes can be streamed anytime on Peacock.",
